WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.410
Joker is officially the highest-grossing R-rated
film of all time, and the star of previous

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.720
champ Deadpool had a couple of choice words
about the development.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.580
The reliably hilarious Ryan Reynolds took
to Instagram to post a mock poster for Joker

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:20.340
offering congrats on behalf of himself and,
well, the subjects of past R-rated box office

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:20.840
smashes.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.220
If you are at all familiar with Reynolds,
you already have a pretty solid idea of what

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.720
to expect, and we can say with certainty that
you won't be disappointed.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.900
Reynolds tagged Joker director Todd Phillips
in the image, and captioned it:

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:37.620
"R-Rated box office congratulatory posts aren't
like the ones you're used to."

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:44.160
No, we should say not, and neither are congratulatory
posts from Deadpool, whom we all know is A)

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.400
kind of insane and B) in no way a fictional
character as long as Reynolds is breathing.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:55.110
There are superhero actors who embody their
roles, and then there is Reynolds, who probably

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.850
sleeps in his costume and has an unhealthy
relationship with his katanas.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.240
"F***, you're old."

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.560
"HAH!

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.740
Fake laugh — hiding real pain.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:05.920
Go get Silver-balls."

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:10.470
For those keeping score at home, the movies
Reynolds refers to at the bottom of the poster

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:18.250
are, in order: Deadpool, The Matrix, It: Chapter
One, The Passion of the Christ, Logan, The

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.360
Hangover, 50 Shades of Grey, and Ted.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:26.360
"Highest-grossing R-rated movie ever" becomes
the latest in a long line of superlatives

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.790
bestowed upon the Joaquin Phoenix starring
Joker since its release, which already include

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:37.240
"biggest October opener of all time," "Golden
Lion award winner," and "odds-on Oscar favorite."

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:42.000
Of course, since they have a slightly narrower
audience, it's a little tougher for R-rated

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:46.790
films to do the kind of bonkers box office
that, say, Marvel Studios' PG-13 offerings

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:47.300
often do.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:53.020
No R-rated flick has ever broken the billion-dollar
mark at the worldwide box office, but Joker

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.760
might very well be the first.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:00.000
In order to even get close, it's done away
with some pretty formidable competition, as

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.140
Reynolds pointed out in his uniquely smartass
fashion.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:08.220
That's one heck of a slate of films that Deadpool
er, Reynolds, rather made reference to on

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:08.980
that poster.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.540
Being huge geeks, we decided to do a little
digging to see just how much box office gold

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.380
they represent.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:19.760
Let's take them in chronological order, starting
with the oldest flick on the list, The Matrix.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:24.020
It's interesting to note that the film came
out about 20 years ago, and its total of just

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:28.300
over $463 million was enough to hand it the
R-rated crown.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:34.260
It was also a bona fide pop culture phenomenon,
spawning two sequels and a multimedia franchise

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:39.270
that includes comic books, video games, and
animated shorts yet, it still couldn't crack

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.920
the half-billion barrier.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:45.840
Adjusted for inflation, though, the total
is closer to $700 million dollars.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:50.860
Next on the list: 2004's The Passion of the
Christ, which benefited from having a pretty

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:55.780
sizable built-in audience and which also dominated
the pop culture conversation in the year of

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:56.560
its release.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:03.560
The flick cleaned up worldwide to the tune
of $610 million $829 million adjusted for

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:07.370
inflation and it stayed on top for a surprisingly
long time.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:11.840
This is because the next two on the list only
earned the title of highest-grossing R-rated

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:12.340
comedy.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:19.080
The Hangover, released in 2009, scored a $468
million worldwide gross, and it held the raunchy

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:25.380
comedy crown until it was bested in 2012 by
Seth McFarlane's Ted, which notched a $549

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.560
million global take.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.410
2015's Fifty Shades of Grey, while a huge
hit, fell short of Passion's total by about

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:35.320
$40 million, making it an outlier on Reynolds'
list.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.730
We're inclined to believe that he's well aware
of this, and threw it in because he wanted

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:43.360
to include a really popular movie with lots
of steamy scenes for a laugh.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.980
If you're unconvinced, we refer you to pretty
much everything the guy has ever posted on

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:48.480
Twitter.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:53.700
It took 12 years and the first, long-awaited
solo vehicle for the Merc with a Mouth to

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:59.370
formally dethrone Jesus, as 2016's Deadpool
smashed all kinds of records en route to a

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:06.220
whopping $782 million or $836 million adjusted
box office total.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.740
That film has technically worn the crown ever
since, as the remaining two movies on Reynolds'

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:14.600
list actually failed to knock it from its
perch.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:20.760
2017's It: Chapter One became the highest-grossing
horror movie of all time with a $700 million

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:26.820
take, while Logan the super-violent swan song
for Reynolds' buddy Hugh Jackman's Wolverine

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.060
only managed $619 million.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:34.840
Logan's inclusion on Reynolds' list was probably
simply a shout-out to his friend or, given

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.340
how much the pair enjoy antagonizing each
other, perhaps it was a mention of a more

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.360
passive-aggressive variety.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:44.340
Logan didn't come close to matching the total
of either Deadpool movie.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:44.980
Whew.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:45.660
OK.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:46.800
Back to Joker.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:48.440
"There.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:49.480
All caught up."

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:56.130
, Joker has raked in an eye-watering $852
million globally and the flick has had some

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.760
extremely long legs.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:02.631
It handily won its first two weekends, came
very close to winning its next two, and its

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:07.240
per-weekend dropoff has been significantly
less pronounced than most tentpole pictures,

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:12.380
including fellow Worlds of DC titles like
Aquaman the only billion-dollar success for

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.580
the franchise so far.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:19.000
It seems only a matter of time before Joker
goes barreling past the billion dollar mark,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.240
and it's tough to imagine that any movie will
challenge it for the R-rated crown anytime

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:23.740
soon.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:29.000
Even Deadpool 3, which is almost certainly
in the works, and Matrix 4, which is definitely

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:34.890
in the works, seem unlikely to score that
big at the box office but if the franchises

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.520
were to team up, they just might pull it off.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.700
Don't try to tell us you know even a single
person who wouldn't pay good money to see

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.220
Deadpool Breaks the Matrix.

